Slide 2: Introduction

• Bullet Points:
	• Conventional CCTV systems function as passive, post-event investigative tools.
	• Human-in-the-loop monitoring introduces high operational latency and frequent oversights.• 
	• SecurEdge-Vision introduces proactive edge-based threat prevention.
	• Combines facial vectorization and object detection on a single edge-computing pipeline.

Slide 3: Problem Statement

• Bullet Points:
	• Cloud Reliance: Current smart security solutions depend entirely on active cloud connections, creating high bandwidth overhead and security vulnerabilities.
	• False Alarms: Standard setups cannot map environmental context, failing to distinguish between everyday visitors (e.g., delivery agents) and true intrusions.
	• Lack of Threat Vision: No native ability within standard camera feeds to immediately isolate weapons (pistols, rifles) or emergency events (fire) at the local frame level.

Slide 4: Project Objectives

• Bullet Points:
	• Build a robust, lightweight 100% cloud-free local vision loop optimized for standard laptops.• 
	• Implement an architecture capable of running concurrent feature extraction and threat detection tasks.
	• Establish a Dynamic Classification Array to categorize individuals based on authorization profiles.
	• Implement a 4-Tier UI Escalation Matrix for tailored real-time alert dispatching.

